  "introStart": "Get started",
  "intro1Title": "Draw a hexagram, read the moment",
  "intro1Body": "Hold one matter in mind and tap Draw a Card on the home screen; on that page you can also choose Cast with Three Coins or Cast with Yarrow Stalks. Each hexagram comes with its judgment and line texts, three readings, a small action and a question to help you think things through.",
  "intro2Title": "Journal: note it, look back",
  "intro2Body": "Save your question and hexagram to the journal; Plum Blossom, Dual Reading, Zi Wei and Bazi results can be saved too. Set a reminder and come back later to see what you thought and how things turned out. You can also back up the journal to a file and restore it on a new phone.",
  "intro3Title": "Breathe with the hexagram",
  "intro3Body": "From a reading you can breathe with the soundscapes of its upper and lower trigrams: in for 4 seconds, out for 6. The background tones and bells are tuned to 432 Hz; with headphones you can turn on a 7.83 Hz binaural beat (the two ears differ by 7.83 Hz). Choose 1, 2, 3 or 5 minutes, or set a custom length of up to 60 minutes for a longer sit.",
  "intro4Title": "Sharing and membership",
  "intro4Body": "Turn a hexagram you like into a card and share it with friends. The texts and readings are always free; the free version gives one cast a day, plus one more after a short ad. Members get no ads, unlimited casts and journal entries, the full Dual Reading, all courses, longer breathing sessions and binaural beats.",
  "intro5Title": "Tell us what you think",
  "intro5Body": "The gear at the top right of the home screen opens Settings: replay this tour, send us feedback, set a daily reminder and choose whether to share anonymous usage stats. Your suggestions help make the app better.",
  "introMeihuaTitle": "Plum Blossom",
  "introMeihuaBody": "Cast from this moment, two numbers or a sentence, then read the situation through the trigram images, self and other, and the nuclear and changed hexagrams, with a five-level trend, a rough time window and ways forward. One time cast a day is free.",
  "introCrossTitle": "Dual Reading",
  "introCrossBody": "Ask one question and cast it with both the I Ching and Plum Blossom. When both point the same way it's agreement; when one is neutral it's a partial echo; otherwise they differ and each keeps its own angle. The reading covers where the two meet, the present moment, the longer arc and ways forward, and adds Zi Wei and Bazi once your birth details are in. The full reading is for members.",
  "introEasternTitle": "Zi Wei · Bazi",
  "introEasternBody": "Enter your birth date and time (kept only on your phone). Zi Wei Dou Shu looks at this year's direction, and Bazi follows the solar terms to look at this month's energy. Each covers one time scale, and both join the Dual Reading. The Life Palace star and Day Master sections are free.",
  "introLearnTitle": "Courses",
  "introLearnBody": "Eight I Ching lessons take you from yin and yang and the trigrams to reading images and changing lines, plus 13 Plum Blossom lessons, 4 on Zi Wei and 3 on Bazi. Every course starts with free lessons, so you can learn to read hexagrams yourself.",
